menu "BMDS kernel"

    config BMDS_ASSERT
        bool "Enable BMDS_ASSERT checks"
        default y
        help
            Compile in BMDS_ASSERT invariant checks. A failed assert panics
            with a backtrace. Disabling saves a little flash and CPU.

    config BMDS_DEBUG_LOG
        bool "Compile in bmdsDebug() logging"
        default y
        help
            Compile in per-module debug logging. Modules are still off at
            runtime until enabled. Disabling removes all debug log strings
            and the module registry.

    config BMDS_LOG_LINE_MAX
        int "Maximum log line length"
        default 160
        range 64 1024
        help
            Size of the on-stack buffer a log line is formatted into.
            Longer lines are truncated.

    config BMDS_LOG_HISTORY_BYTES
        int "Log history size (bytes, PSRAM)"
        default 65536
        range 0 1048576
        help
            Size of the ring that keeps recent log text for 'log show' and for the log files
            (devplan/logging.md: the lines from before the card mounts).
            Allocated from PSRAM at boot. 0 disables the history.

    config BMDS_PIPE_BYTES
        int "Pipe buffer size (bytes, PSRAM)"
        default 4096
        range 256 65536
        help
            Ring size of each pipe between pipeline stages. Must be a power
            of two. Allocated from PSRAM when the pipeline starts and freed
            when it ends.

    config BMDS_TIMEZONE
        string "Kernel time zone (POSIX TZ string or zone name)"
        default "UTC0"
        help
            The time zone the kernel shows time in and stamps FAT files
            with (FAT stores local time). A POSIX TZ string, e.g.
            "CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3" or "EST5EDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0", or
            a name in the time zone database on the card, e.g.
            "Europe/Berlin" (UTC until the card's database is found).
            The default of the system configuration's clock/zone, which
            'sysconf' changes at run time.
            The clock itself keeps UTC; the shell's TZ variable overrides
            the zone for display.

endmenu
